       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 10,000 mg three times daily is 30 g/day, which is more than 7 times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for an adult. A single 10 g dose is already in the range that can cause severe hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function. For a 70 kg patient, the toxic threshold is about 150 mg/kg, or roughly 10.5 g.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day), which is a common regimen.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day).\n- **500 mg to 1,000 mg PO every 6 to 8 hours**, with a total of 4 g/day or less.\n\nIf you want the 10,000 mg dose for a reason I'm not aware of, tell me the clinical context. I'd still advise against entering it as written. Give me the corrected dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
