       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. A dose of 10,000 mg three times daily (30 g/day) is a potentially lethal overdose. I can't find any clinical scenario where it would be appropriate for a 70 kg adult. Acetaminophen toxicity can cause fulminant liver failure, and normal baseline liver and kidney function doesn't protect against it at this dose.\n\nHere is what I can do instead:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1,000 mg PO four times daily (the 4 g/day maximum). Tell me which one you want.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 1,000 mg, or 650 mg, I can enter that.\n- **Route this through pharmacy.** If you have a specific protocol in mind, such as a research or unusual clinical protocol, the pharmacy and your institution's medication safety process can review and verify it.\n\nLet me know which you'd like."
      }
